  ($qb$S03C07Q01$qb$, $qb$S03$qb$, $qb$C07$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Interpersonal conflicts within teams in your organisation are managed by:$qb$, $qb$Direct and early intervention — managers address conflict when it emerges, not when it has escalated$qb$, $qb$Eventual intervention — managers address serious conflicts but allow minor ones to persist longer than ideal$qb$, $qb$Avoidance — managers do not address interpersonal conflicts directly and hope they resolve themselves$qb$, $qb$Non-management — interpersonal conflicts are not seen as a management responsibility and are left unresolved$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
